      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds great for the high-level stuff, but the investors are going to dig into the actual data. They're going to ask about the p-values. I saw the report mentioned it was 0.06. How should I frame that so they don't get hung up on it and worry about the lack of statistical significance?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
